    "lang": "en",
    "score": null
  },
  {
    "id": "2110919225459998776",
    "text": "You may save money in the short term, at the expense of worse work at the end. That doesn't mean small models can't do tons of valuable work, but you want to make sure they are orchestrated and error-checked by larger ones for many kinds of tasks.\n\nPaper: https://t.co/D557qQbs5g",
    "author": {
      "id": "39125788",
      "name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "screenName": "emollick",
      "profileImageUrl": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1601382188712398850/3AAOlqrX_normal.jpg",
      "verified": true
    },
    "metrics": {
      "likes": 92,
      "retweets": 8,
      "replies": 10,
      "quotes": 1,
      "views": 15130,
      "bookmarks": 19
    },
    "createdAt": "Fri Oct 16 02:22:16 +0000 2026",
    "createdAtLocal": "2026-10-16 10:22",
    "createdAtISO": "2026-10-16T02:22:16+00:00",
    "media": [],
    "urls": [
      "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2509.09677"
    ],
    "isRetweet": false,
    "retweetedBy": null,
    "lang": "en",
    "score": null
  },
  {
    "id": "2111048324291899785",
    "text": "I should also point out that almost all benchmarks are of  single-answer short-horizon tasks, but a large amount of economically valuable work is complex long-horizon tasks. Again, there is room for both, but I think we will find \"good enough\" intelligence may not always be.",
    "author": {
      "id": "39125788",
      "name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "screenName": "emollick",
      "profileImageUrl": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1601382188712398850/3AAOlqrX_normal.jpg",
      "verified": true
    },
